Bug: a header changed on disk leaves ghosts in its other includers

definer.c and user.c both include header.h. When header.h is rewritten on disk with
the declaration moved, a push in definer.c finds the declaration on line 3, but the
reference to line 1 of the old header.h stays. Both CUs put it there.

Cause: nothing makes a CU out of date when a header it includes changes on disk. Pass 2
looks only at headers held in the editor.

Fix: ADR-0032. header.h is an input of both CUs, so their knowledge is out of date and
both are built again. The references in header.h are removed first, which ADR-0032
allows when all of its includers are built (all or nothing). The work is section 7 of
doc/backlog.md, items knowledge-time, cu-inputs and out-of-date, wired in by
passes-as-one, which takes this test off suspension.
